WEBVTT
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.000
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]


00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.400
Mi Young.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.210
Mi Young.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.210
Get the staff to handle any physical labour.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.280
You should get some rest.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:17.980
Especially since you are expecting.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.650
I am really fine.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.490
Everyone is so busy. How can I just sit around and do nothing?

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.160
Oh, hello.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.760
Did you like the dresses you tried on last time?

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.260
- Yes. - We have many more new designs,

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.000
so you can try them all on and make your final decision...

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.570
Hey, are you busy?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.370
Can't you tell? I do not even have time to use the restroom.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.110
But about Mi Young...

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.640
Is she going to be okay working like this?

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.940
Mi Young? What about her?

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.280
It is our peak season, so we are swamped with work,

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.720
but she is pregnant.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.020
I am worried she is pushing herself too hard.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.020
Oh, you are right.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.090
Come to think of it, I have been so busy...

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.860
I have not paid any attention to her these last few days.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.290
I should tell her to go home and rest. Right?

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.490
She will just refuse to go.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.160
Then what do I do? Just let her overdo it?

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.370
How about getting her some herbal medicine?

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.400
Herbal medicine?

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.170
You know that oriental medicine clinic you go to.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.740
- Yes. - Get some for Mi Young there?

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.340
Yes. That is a good idea. And the doctor there is trustworthy.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.510
Hey, you are more thoughtful than me.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.820
(Daehyeon Oriental Medicine Clinic)

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.890
Hello. I am here to pick up some herbal medicine.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:31.960
Okay, and the name is?

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.260
The order should be under Ji Won Ho.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.690
I am just picking it up for him.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.530
Okay, one moment.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.370
Okay, here you are.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.440
Thank you.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:51.140
That is everything.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:55.610
I gave that same herbal medicine to Mi Young.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:03.350
But did that medicine really cause Mi Young to...

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.560
No. I think there must have been a mix-up.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:08.830
You do not have to worry about it anymore.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:09.890
Go on. Get back to work.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:11.930
Okay, then.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.660
(Episode 9)

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.840
- There. - There what?

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:24.740
You just heard what Kyung Tae said.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.980
The medicine you took three years ago...

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.810
was perfectly fine medicine, brought straight from the clinic.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.280
So the misunderstanding is all cleared up now, right?

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.020
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.850
We lost Dallae because of that medicine.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.060
When you first said we lost Dallae because of the medicine,

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:43.860
I never even thought it could be the herbal medicine.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:44.930
Do you know why?

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.100
Because there was zero chance of it causing any problems.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.730
I told them you were pregnant and asked them...

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.400
to be especially careful with it.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.870
I checked with the doctor again and again...

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.570
before I brought that medicine to you.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:57.910
I was not supposed to take that medicine.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.610
Then you should have told me at the time.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.110
Let us assume you are right, and it was the medicine.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.250
But what do you want me to do about it now?

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:08.550
It has been three years. What is there to do now?

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.250
Apologise.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.620
- What? - Because of your mistake,

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.020
we lost Dallae.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.530
I want you to finally repent and apologize for it.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.430
Apologise to Dallae!

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.500
What difference will that make?

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.040
Will that bring our dead Dallae back to life?

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.710
Get out. I said get out.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.010
Do not worry, I am leaving.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:57.870
(Vice President Kang Kyung Tae)

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.270
Mr. Kang Kyung Tae.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.570
What is it?

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:09.310
I would like to ask you some questions about this.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:14.880
Let's talk outside.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:25.260
I went that day because I was so worried.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:29.400
I was worried you were up to something bad again.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:30.730
What did you say?

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.940
The scandal photos of CEO Baek and Calvin...

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:34.840
was your doing, wasn't it?

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.210
Because of that, not only CEO Baek,

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.440
but our company was at risk.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.380
But then the person behind it all suddenly joined our company,

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.950
and said the first photo shoot would be at a cliff.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.020
As the vice president, how could I not be worried?

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.990
That must be why you pushed me off the cliff.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:01.660
Excuse me. I never pushed you off that cliff.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.900
But I have clear proof right here.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:10.210
I told you. The wind was so strong...

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.040
that I only went up to that point and turned back.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.350
Besides, this can't be used as proof.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.520
It's not like it shows me pushing you off the cliff.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.620
May I go now?

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.970
If it's true someone pushed you off that cliff,

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.880
do you really think they'll stop there?

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.380
What do you mean?

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:50.850
They'll probably come...

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.850
after you again, don't you think?

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.560
Since they haven't achieved their goal yet.

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:05.090
So try to lay low.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.370
Watch your back.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.890
I just need the official seal stamped here.

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:34.690
The vice president has the official seal,

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.590
but he's not here right now.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.690
Oh, really?

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.360
Do I have to come all the way back just for this?

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.130
One moment. Please wait.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:16.500
I really am a genius. All right.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.510
Okay.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.190
- Director Song. - Yes.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.990
The client is in a hurry and needs you now.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.760
- Okay. I'm on my way down. - Yes, Director Song.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.200
It just doesn't make sense.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:53.370
The person who took the medicine got sick,

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:56.170
but the one who gave it to her is completely blameless.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:58.010
You don't think I'd actually give her medicine...

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.080
that would harm her, do you?

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:00.740
Well, that is strange.

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:03.710
The medicine couldn't have become poisonous on its own.

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.080
My wife is the one who's full of poison.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:07.750
She held onto that for three years,

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.450
and now she's unleashing all that venom on me.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:11.690
Just to make me suffer.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.660
Your wife is doing this just to make you suffer?

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:15.830
What else could it be?

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.460
Why she'd make me look like a fool for three years, then?

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.230
I don't know...

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:23.000
- We should drag this out longer. - Pardon?

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.240
Let's say...

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.340
what your wife is saying is true, what will you do?

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:34.640
- What are you... - What if you...

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:39.650
- were a real murderer? - What are you talking about?

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:41.850
Hey, I told you to control that temper.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:44.650
Sit down. You need to hear me out first.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.530
Let's calm down and think this through rationally.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.300
You gave your wife medicine that was perfectly fine.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.900
But what is your wife claiming?

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:02.610
That she lost the baby because of that medicine.

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:04.570
But let me ask you again.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:08.280
Is there any particular reason...

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:11.080
you're so sure of your innocence?

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.380
How many times do I have to say it?

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:15.180
I never gave my wife any medicine that could harm her,

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:16.590
and I had no reason to.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.650
But listen.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:21.820
Life doesn't always go according to your plans...

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:24.890
or your intentions.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.900
Unexpected variables and accidents...

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:34.940
actually happen more often than you'd think.

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:40.410
So you're saying I should keep an open mind...

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.510
and consider other possibilities?

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.150
Exactly.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:47.950
Even a fire that seems to be out...

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:51.050
isn't really out.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.030
- But, Counsellor... - Yes?

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.800
I think you should probably put out that fire first.

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:13.010
Oh, it's ruined...

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:19.850
So was it really the medicine...

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:21.380
your husband gave you that caused it?

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:22.850
But...

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.260
my husband swears it wasn't.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:27.960
I don't understand.

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.760
Of course you don't.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:32.130
My husband and I...

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.800
have an absurd relationship.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:40.470
At work, we're business partners.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:44.910
Outside of work, we're enemies suing for divorce.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.650
But you know what's really upsetting?

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:54.980
It's that my husband...

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.820
has already forgotten all about it.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.220
Whenever I try to bring it up,

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.860
he always gets angry.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.630
He asks why I'm still talking about our child who died.

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:11.470
And why...

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.640
am I still stuck in that moment?

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:21.410
Whenever he says that,

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.650
I feel like he's blaming me.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.090
It's still...

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:35.120
torment for me whenever I think about that day.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:41.400
This torment...

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.200
feels like it will never end.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.510
But not my husband.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.010
He's...

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:57.680
completely different from me.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.420
He probably...

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:01.820
hasn't forgotten.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:04.850
The truth is,

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.390
I still haven't cleared out my kid's room.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:13.100
It's been one year since his mom took him and left,

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:15.530
but his room...

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.100
is exactly the way it was one year ago.

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:21.140
If I didn't at least do that,

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:22.910
I don't think...

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:25.910
I could bear the feeling of that loss.

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:32.520
Are you okay?

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:38.220
I'm sorry.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.220
How silly of me.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:54.840
Won Ho.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.910
I'll have a beer, too, please.

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:01.940
Thanks.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:06.020
Why are you drinking alone? You should've called me.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:08.080
Kyung Tae.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.150
I have a feeling this whole thing...

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.120
will just remain an unsolved mystery.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.130
An unsolved mystery?

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:18.530
I went to the herbal medicine clinic today.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:22.500
I wanted to see if there was really something...

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.230
wrong with the herbal medicine from back then.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:26.500
And?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.070
Did you find anything out?

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.510
Just as I thought. They said there was nothing wrong with it.

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:35.140
And that there's no way...

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:36.650
it could have caused the miscarriage.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.350
Then what is it? Seriously.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:44.950
Mi Young isn't the type to just make things up for no reason.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:47.690
She's just not over it yet, I guess.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.530
Over it?

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.700
I think she just wants to blame me for everything that happened...

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:55.100
around the time of the miscarriage.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.400
The volunteer work with Father Kwon...

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.670
and the medicine.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.010
Honestly, that's a bit of a stretch.

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:05.510
If she thought it was all her fault,

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.180
she wouldn't be able to bear it.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.920
Mi Young wanted Dallae to be born more than anything.

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:19.520
And you didn't feel the same?

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:21.860
You both felt that way.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:30.430
But...

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.540
if you just let this go,

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:34.740
won't that put you in a tough spot?

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:37.510
Mi Young will keep blaming you...

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.510
all the way up to the trial.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.340
I don't care about that.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:46.750
The problem is she's the one having a harder time.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:04.500
Hey. Why does it feel so stuffy in here?

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.700
Is it because I ate that sweet potato?

00:15:07.770 --> 00:15:08.770
No.

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:11.040
It has nothing to do with the sweet potato.

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.780
It's because it's too cramped in here.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:15.780
Because of a certain someone.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.750
Hey. It's CEO Ji.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.060
What took you so long?

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.190
I've been waiting.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:28.890
What were you doing sitting there?

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:31.930
Take her with you.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:35.730
Let's go.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.040
Kyung Tae pushed you off a cliff?

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:43.210
Yes.

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:46.410
The one who's always stuck to you like glue.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.940
I met him and asked him about it myself today.

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.410
And he just confessed?

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:53.480
Of course he said no.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.050
But he threatened me.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:59.590
He told me not to get carried away and to watch myself.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:02.420
Come on. That's not a threat. That's just advice.

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:05.960
- What? - Stop. It's not Kyung Tae.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.500
I'm telling you, he's the one.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:12.600
- Unbelievable. - About the scandal photos I took,

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:14.900
did you tell him about them?

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:16.610
Scandal photos?

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:17.970
You know.

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:20.280
The ones I took and showed you...

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.240
of Calvin and your wife.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.280
The pictures from the scandal article.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:25.850
He said...

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:27.650
if I knew how much trouble the employees went through...

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:30.590
because I took those pictures.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.790
No, there's no way Kyung Tae would know about that.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.920
I'm telling you, that guy is really suspicious.

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:38.330
Fine, you're right about everything.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:41.230
You're right, so hurry up and go. I'm tired.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.770
No, I'm sleeping here.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.370
- What? - I told you, I was threatened.

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:49.640
I'm too scared to sleep alone.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:58.980
Okay, then here's the plan.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:02.120
My brother and mom come in and out of here sometimes,

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:03.690
so let's go to your room.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.520
Really?

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:09.390
You said you're this scared, so I'll stay with you tonight.

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:12.630
Then should we go to my room and order chicken?

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:14.160
Yes, eat a lot.

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:17.200
What are you doing?

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:19.500
You can't do this.

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:21.270
Open the door.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.640
Stop fooling around and stay in your room.

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:24.110
Lock your door and go to bed.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:27.310
I'm telling you, I'm really scared by myself.

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:47.730
Were you scared, Princess Dallae?

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.870
Daddy's right here, so don't worry.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:54.540
Daddy will protect our princesses.

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.000
Kiss.

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:35.910
I'm sure that was the brooch.

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:38.910
This is so pretty.

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:41.980
Won Ho has such great taste.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.490
He bought you this as a gift to celebrate your pregnancy.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:45.950
While he was on his business trip to Milan,

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.390
he said he thought of me and bought it.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:50.490
Give me a break. You're making me jealous.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:52.690
I was trying to make you jealous.

00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:54.430
What?

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:57.100
- Take it off. Let me try it on. - No, it's mine.

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:59.600
The brooch that Mi Young lost...

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.440
Why is it in Vice President Kang's drawer?

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.510
(Vice President Kang Kyung Tae)

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:12.980
(Vice President Kang Kyung Tae)

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:15.120
Vice President Kang.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:18.590
- Yes? - Can I talk to you for a moment?

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:27.630
Say that again. What did you just say to me?

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:30.870
I told you I'll agree to your terms for the division of assets.

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:32.630
No, the part after that.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:34.800
In exchange for the assets, you want what?

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.070
That I never mention the medication again?

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:38.940
And the topic of the miscarriage.

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.910
Let's leave that out of the trial and just focus on other things.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.280
And why should I do that?

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:45.350
You have plenty of other complaints about me.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.850
So why bring up such a sensitive topic on top of everything else?

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:49.420
Since we're getting divorced anyway,

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:51.420
let's just try to resolve this smoothly.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.520
Besides, it's not like you have anything to lose.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:56.090
Think about how much money you'll save just by holding your tongue.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:01.660
Director Song.

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:03.230
Are you asking me...

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:05.400
if I stole something?

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:09.040
I didn't do it on purpose.

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:13.380
I was looking for the company seal, and by pure coincidence,

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:17.380
I happened to see inside your drawer.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.180
The brooch...

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:21.920
that CEO Baek lost several years ago...

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.820
was in there.

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:27.560
Of all things, the same brooch that disappeared into thin air.

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:29.830
You saw inside my drawer by coincidence?

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:33.400
I'm sure it was locked. How was it a coincidence?

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:34.930
I told you.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:38.400
I had no choice because of the seal.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.040
I opened it. I found the key.

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:46.240
So the person who opened my drawer without permission...

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:48.880
is now accusing me of being a thief.

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:52.980
But as for opening the drawer, it really was because of the seal...

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:55.620
Does that give you the right to go through someone's things?

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:57.890
Apologise.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.820
I wasn't trying to go through your things.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:03.690
Why are you getting angry?

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:05.830
You're treating an innocent person like a thief.

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:07.460
How do you expect me not to be angry?

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.870
I was just asking.

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:12.130
You weren't just asking.

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:14.440
Apologise properly.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:18.770
- I'm sorry. - Is that what you call an apology?

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:21.780
- I just apologised. - Did you just speak informally?

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:23.750
What does it matter if my speech is formal or informal?

00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:25.710
I apologised, and that should be enough.

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:28.680
If I was going to be nice and settle this easily with you,

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:29.950
do you think I would have filed a lawsuit?

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.890
So you're really determined to see this through to the bitter end?

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:34.690
Who was it that first used the division of assets as bait...

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:36.730
to try and shut me up?

00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:40.800
Hey, will you spend the rest of your life thinking about Dallae?

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:43.270
How could you, who completely forgot about Dallae,

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.070
possibly know how I feel?

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:48.040
What?

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:50.740
To you, Dallae, who you never even carried,

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.040
meant nothing.

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:54.380
And you?

00:21:55.510 --> 00:21:56.550
Did you get to hold her?

00:21:58.450 --> 00:22:00.320
Because of a child you never even gave birth to or raised,

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.920
for you to be like this for years...

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:04.450
is just being overly dramatic.

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:06.120
Overly dramatic?

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:08.190
How could you...

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:10.760
How could you say that to me?

00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:14.100
So just let her go now.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:19.870
Why are you acting like this?

00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:22.270
It's time to let her go.

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:25.410
Mi Young.

00:22:27.710 --> 00:22:28.710
Are you okay?

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:34.320
What are you doing here without calling?

00:22:34.550 --> 00:22:35.880
I see this happens often.

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:38.990
- What? - Mi Young is over there crying,

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:40.960
and you don't seem bothered at all.

00:22:41.060 --> 00:22:42.860
Why are you here again?

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:44.260
Just fire...

00:22:45.190 --> 00:22:46.330
Mi Young.

00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:48.130
Fire her?

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.230
I can no longer leave her by your side.

00:22:51.070 --> 00:22:52.200
Not as your business partner,

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.140
and not as your spouse.

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:56.640
Of course,

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:58.740
your marriage will be over soon anyway.

00:23:00.580 --> 00:23:01.580
No.

00:23:02.740 --> 00:23:04.110
I'm not going to fire her.

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:08.380
You've been doing this since last time.

00:23:09.890 --> 00:23:11.120
Is crossing the line a hobby of yours?

00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:13.660
Do I look like a pushover to you?

00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:14.960
Do I?

00:23:16.090 --> 00:23:17.160
And you?

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:19.360
You said you'd make Mi Young happy,

00:23:20.260 --> 00:23:22.460
but you just make her cry like this every day.

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:26.100
How would you know if she cries or laughs every day?

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:29.000
She cried yesterday too...

00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:30.770
because of you.

00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:34.010
Do you get it now?

00:23:34.710 --> 00:23:35.740
Mi Young...

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:38.710
is only miserable when she's with you.

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:57.670
Thank you for everything.

00:23:58.230 --> 00:23:59.470
Don't mention it.

00:24:00.970 --> 00:24:03.410
By the way, about my younger brother and his wife,

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:05.410
how is their lawsuit coming along?

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:08.440
The lawsuit is taking a bit longer than expected.

00:24:09.210 --> 00:24:10.210
Right now, we're waiting for...

00:24:10.280 --> 00:24:11.710
the second Domestic Affairs Investigation.

00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:13.150
Domestic Affairs Investigation?

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:14.850
That's an important step.

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:16.490
How do you know that?

00:24:16.820 --> 00:24:17.850
Actually, I...

00:24:18.390 --> 00:24:20.720
have some experience with it. I'm divorced.

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:22.890
It's been five years for me.

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:25.190
Actually, I'm divorced too.

00:24:26.090 --> 00:24:27.660
Mine is much more recent.

00:24:29.500 --> 00:24:31.670
- It's only been one year. - Oh, really?

00:24:32.230 --> 00:24:33.340
Why are you so surprised?

00:24:33.440 --> 00:24:35.800
I don't know who he is, but the man who let you get away...

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:37.070
must have been out of his mind.

00:24:37.870 --> 00:24:39.210
Letting go of someone so lovely...

00:24:43.350 --> 00:24:44.410
Duck.

00:24:45.350 --> 00:24:46.380
Quick.

00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:54.860
Seung Ho, where did he go? He's not at his desk again.

00:24:55.020 --> 00:24:57.560
Is he on the rooftop grilling something again?

00:24:57.690 --> 00:24:59.490
Oh, that big boy.

00:25:20.380 --> 00:25:21.420
Ahn Hee Ju.

00:25:21.650 --> 00:25:22.780
Is this the best you can do?

00:25:23.220 --> 00:25:26.020
- Excuse me? - Here. The faces of these two.

00:25:26.220 --> 00:25:27.690
Look at the difference in brightness.

00:25:27.920 --> 00:25:29.660
The bride's face is completely washed out,

00:25:29.660 --> 00:25:30.760
and the groom next to her is...

00:25:31.730 --> 00:25:34.230
Why am I the one having to explain this to a photographer?

00:25:34.960 --> 00:25:36.300
I know you got this job through connections,

00:25:36.360 --> 00:25:38.000
but that's no excuse for this kind of work.

00:25:38.470 --> 00:25:40.540
Fix this properly, and bring it back to me.

00:25:50.210 --> 00:25:53.280
What was that? Are they about to fight?

00:25:58.790 --> 00:25:59.860
Won Ho!

00:25:59.920 --> 00:26:00.920
Where are you going?

00:26:03.260 --> 00:26:05.360
Where could he be going at this hour?

00:26:05.690 --> 00:26:06.700
Hey.

00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:10.800
What do you think you're doing?

00:26:10.970 --> 00:26:13.200
I just gave you an assignment.

00:26:13.770 --> 00:26:17.340
You think by doing this, I'm just going to give up?

00:26:17.870 --> 00:26:18.870
No.

00:26:18.940 --> 00:26:21.010
I'm going to prove...

00:26:21.110 --> 00:26:24.750
that you were the one who tried to push me off that cliff.

00:26:25.010 --> 00:26:26.480
You're going to run out of time.

00:26:26.920 --> 00:26:27.920
What did you say?

00:26:28.020 --> 00:26:31.450
Hurry up, and finish your work by the end of today.

00:26:36.930 --> 00:26:38.860
Darn it, this is so frustrating.

00:26:39.160 --> 00:26:41.730
What am I going to do with him? Seriously.

00:26:45.700 --> 00:26:47.140
The cliff...

00:26:52.170 --> 00:26:53.580
Still feeling down?

00:26:54.840 --> 00:26:57.180
Excuse me? What do you mean, sir?

00:26:57.910 --> 00:27:00.220
I'm asking if you're still having a hard time.

00:27:07.060 --> 00:27:08.920
Rest easy before you go.

00:27:31.280 --> 00:27:32.580
Darn it...

00:27:48.600 --> 00:27:50.370
- Take care of this. - Yes.

00:27:52.970 --> 00:27:54.170
Are you heading out now?

00:27:54.640 --> 00:27:57.670
I'm not feeling well, so I'm going to leave early today.

00:27:57.810 --> 00:27:59.810
Can you please close up for me later?

00:28:00.010 --> 00:28:02.210
Of course. Go on and get some rest.

00:28:02.510 --> 00:28:03.550
Thank you.

00:28:04.580 --> 00:28:05.580
Mi Young.

00:28:06.850 --> 00:28:07.850
You...

00:28:08.550 --> 00:28:11.990
know that brooch from a while back?

00:28:12.420 --> 00:28:15.690
The one you lost a few years ago when you were working off-site.

00:28:15.920 --> 00:28:17.360
Did you ever find it?

00:28:17.690 --> 00:28:20.060
No, I never did.

00:28:20.730 --> 00:28:23.160
But why are you asking about the brooch all of a sudden?

00:28:23.430 --> 00:28:24.530
What?

00:28:24.800 --> 00:28:28.870
Oh, no reason. It just popped into my head.

00:28:30.810 --> 00:28:32.810
- I'm leaving. - Okay.

00:28:37.810 --> 00:28:40.080
No matter how I think about it,

00:28:40.150 --> 00:28:42.620
I'm sure it's the same brooch...

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.640
Are you all right?

00:29:02.270 --> 00:29:03.270
What?

00:29:06.110 --> 00:29:08.440
You must have been really startled earlier.

00:29:08.740 --> 00:29:11.550
No. I was more worried about you.

00:29:12.510 --> 00:29:13.880
When I saw you crying,

00:29:14.050 --> 00:29:15.480
I was very concerned.

00:29:16.720 --> 00:29:19.390
It's okay. You don't have to worry about it anymore.

00:29:19.850 --> 00:29:22.920
Oh, right. Why did you come by our company earlier?

00:29:35.670 --> 00:29:36.910
Gosh...

00:29:43.110 --> 00:29:44.910
My company is thinking about...

00:29:44.980 --> 00:29:46.920
establishing a wedding-related subsidiary.

00:29:47.150 --> 00:29:49.280
A total wedding service company, like J&White.

00:29:50.550 --> 00:29:51.720
That's great.

00:29:52.050 --> 00:29:53.560
You already have...

00:29:53.560 --> 00:29:55.760
all the wedding hall infrastructure in place, right?

00:29:56.220 --> 00:29:58.890
A wedding company under the Calvin brand...

00:29:59.260 --> 00:30:00.730
That's a really great idea.

00:30:01.330 --> 00:30:02.900
I've thought about it a lot.

00:30:03.430 --> 00:30:06.130
I know how much passion and responsibility...

00:30:06.200 --> 00:30:07.970
you have for J&White.

00:30:09.840 --> 00:30:10.910
But...

00:30:11.110 --> 00:30:13.170
I think I can confidently make my offer now.

00:30:14.740 --> 00:30:17.350
I want you to take the CEO position...

00:30:18.710 --> 00:30:20.180
at the new Calvin Wedding.

00:30:57.890 --> 00:30:59.390
Dallae, have you been well?

00:31:00.820 --> 00:31:02.190
You haven't been cold, have you?

00:31:06.030 --> 00:31:07.430
You haven't forgotten Daddy's face...

00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:09.100
just because it's been a while, right?

00:31:12.470 --> 00:31:15.200
Come to think of it, time really flies.

00:31:17.670 --> 00:31:20.340
It's already been three years...

00:31:22.180 --> 00:31:24.180
since I had to say goodbye to you, my Dallae.

00:31:30.850 --> 00:31:32.090
(Authorized Personnel Only)

00:31:33.390 --> 00:31:35.790
(Operating Room)

00:31:58.510 --> 00:32:00.650
(Rest in Peace)

00:32:03.250 --> 00:32:06.790
(Cremation Room)

00:32:15.260 --> 00:32:16.700
What am I going to do...

00:32:27.940 --> 00:32:30.950
Wait. Just a moment. Let me think about it one more time.

00:32:31.010 --> 00:32:32.210
I think...

00:32:32.510 --> 00:32:34.880
I think it will be too hot for the baby.

00:34:15.680 --> 00:34:17.720
People probably don't know...

00:34:18.650 --> 00:34:20.150
that when the warm spring comes,

00:34:20.220 --> 00:34:22.490
what beautiful flowers bloom here.

00:34:24.160 --> 00:34:27.900
And how much Daddy misses our Dallae.

00:34:29.830 --> 00:34:31.400
And how much I long to see you again.

00:34:35.670 --> 00:34:37.140
But it's okay if they don't know.

00:34:40.740 --> 00:34:42.140
As long as you...

00:34:45.650 --> 00:34:48.050
All that matters is you understand how Daddy feels.

00:35:02.460 --> 00:35:05.100
Where could he have gone on such an important day?

00:35:09.970 --> 00:35:11.270
What's going on?

00:35:11.540 --> 00:35:14.310
I guess CEO Ji isn't answering his phone.

00:35:14.410 --> 00:35:15.880
He didn't show up for work yesterday without notice,

00:35:16.280 --> 00:35:17.780
and now he's completely dropped off the map.

00:35:19.180 --> 00:35:21.120
Today is the Domestic Affairs Investigation,

00:35:21.320 --> 00:35:22.780
so he absolutely has to be there.

00:35:23.080 --> 00:35:26.420
Oh, I see.

00:35:28.390 --> 00:35:29.990
Why are you looking at me like that?

00:35:30.290 --> 00:35:33.590
- Worried I might've stolen again? - No, that's not it.

00:35:35.330 --> 00:35:37.100
The person you have called is currently on another line.

00:35:37.100 --> 00:35:38.900
- After the tone... - What? Come on.

00:35:42.170 --> 00:35:44.970
Well, I answered your call, didn't I?

00:35:45.170 --> 00:35:46.970
I haven't been answering anyone else's,

00:35:47.040 --> 00:35:49.610
but I made an exception for you, Counsellor.

00:35:49.680 --> 00:35:51.750
My, I'm so honoured.

00:35:51.810 --> 00:35:54.150
Should I bow down in gratitude?

00:35:54.220 --> 00:35:55.550
I'm serious.

00:35:55.620 --> 00:35:58.450
My point exactly. Seriously, what's wrong with you?

00:35:58.920 --> 00:36:01.660
You're supposed to be winning over the Family Affairs Investigator,

00:36:01.720 --> 00:36:03.490
not out here catching fish.

00:36:03.830 --> 00:36:05.990
It just kind of happened that way.

00:36:06.130 --> 00:36:07.530
Just go now.

00:36:07.760 --> 00:36:10.570
The Domestic Affairs Investigation starts at 2pm

00:36:10.670 --> 00:36:12.600
Even if you're late, race over there.

00:36:13.900 --> 00:36:15.000
I'm not going.

00:36:15.340 --> 00:36:17.140
It'll just be hard on both of us if I go.

00:36:17.910 --> 00:36:21.110
Today, it's better if we just avoid each other.

00:36:21.310 --> 00:36:23.380
What in the world is so important about today?

00:36:32.720 --> 00:36:35.420
Since your husband failed to appear,

00:36:35.590 --> 00:36:37.690
it will be difficult to proceed.

00:36:39.130 --> 00:36:40.130
I understand.

00:36:41.030 --> 00:36:43.800
In that case, you can go home for today,

00:36:43.930 --> 00:36:46.330
and we'll schedule another appointment.

00:36:50.640 --> 00:36:53.710
I hated being alone.

00:36:55.180 --> 00:36:56.180
I'm sorry?

00:36:58.710 --> 00:37:00.450
In this vast, cold world,

00:37:01.820 --> 00:37:03.280
I felt like I'd been thrown out all alone.

00:37:07.560 --> 00:37:08.560
It was...

00:37:10.260 --> 00:37:12.090
so frightening and scary.

00:37:16.530 --> 00:37:19.530
I lost my parents, who were my only family,

00:37:20.540 --> 00:37:22.400
both at once in an accident.

00:37:24.610 --> 00:37:26.670
I became an orphan overnight,

00:37:27.910 --> 00:37:28.910
and once again,

00:37:30.710 --> 00:37:32.580
I went through a miserable ordeal.

00:37:53.940 --> 00:37:54.940
For a long time,

00:37:56.070 --> 00:37:58.570
I was completely closed off because of my pain.

00:38:00.440 --> 00:38:02.110
But the one who opened my heart...

00:38:05.750 --> 00:38:07.150
was my husband.

00:38:09.120 --> 00:38:10.120
And...

00:38:15.160 --> 00:38:17.230
the child who came to me like a miracle.

00:38:18.930 --> 00:38:20.660
When I was pregnant with our child,

00:38:23.060 --> 00:38:25.130
I felt like I had been born again.

00:38:27.540 --> 00:38:29.140
For that child's sake,

00:38:30.640 --> 00:38:33.670
there was nothing in the world to be afraid of.

00:38:35.740 --> 00:38:36.910
For that child,

00:38:40.010 --> 00:38:41.920
I would have gladly died.

00:38:44.890 --> 00:38:46.290
As a mother,

00:38:47.990 --> 00:38:48.990
I thought I could do...

00:38:52.330 --> 00:38:54.430
anything at all.

00:38:57.160 --> 00:38:58.170
I really did.

00:39:01.640 --> 00:39:02.840
But, Investigator,

00:39:05.040 --> 00:39:06.040
where do you think...

00:39:08.610 --> 00:39:10.280
that child is now?

00:39:14.750 --> 00:39:16.380
After I die...

00:39:18.090 --> 00:39:19.090
No...

00:39:21.920 --> 00:39:23.460
Even in the next life,

00:39:25.890 --> 00:39:27.560
will I be able to see her again?

00:39:39.610 --> 00:39:40.710
Hello.

00:39:41.240 --> 00:39:42.480
Yes, please come in.

00:39:47.580 --> 00:39:48.980
Have you been well?

00:39:50.120 --> 00:39:51.650
Well, look who it is.

00:39:52.620 --> 00:39:53.620
Jeon Chi Hyun?

00:39:54.720 --> 00:39:57.060
Or is it Attorney Jeon Chi Hyun?

00:39:58.130 --> 00:40:01.100
My, you remembered my name.

00:40:02.330 --> 00:40:03.630
Of course, I do.

00:40:04.330 --> 00:40:06.430
Just a moment, it's a bit of a mess.

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:09.070
Oh, goodness.

00:40:10.200 --> 00:40:11.210
Darn it.

00:40:14.810 --> 00:40:15.840
Have a seat.

00:40:18.010 --> 00:40:19.380
Oh, boy.

00:40:20.250 --> 00:40:21.620
How long has it been?

00:40:22.450 --> 00:40:24.190
You were really something back then.

00:40:24.690 --> 00:40:27.690
You took such a beating from me, but got right back up.

00:40:27.860 --> 00:40:29.120
I'd knock you down again and again.

00:40:29.360 --> 00:40:31.260
You even ended up losing your office.

00:40:31.390 --> 00:40:33.160
Who said I was the one getting knocked down?

00:40:33.330 --> 00:40:37.130
Well, whatever. It certainly wasn't me.

00:40:38.130 --> 00:40:40.670
I tried my best to be patient,

00:40:41.100 --> 00:40:42.570
but don't you think this is going too far?

00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:44.510
Going too far? What is?

00:40:44.710 --> 00:40:46.210
You were the one who scheduled the second...

00:40:46.270 --> 00:40:47.610
Domestic Affairs Investigation date.

00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:50.610
- So? - But to not show up without notice?

00:40:51.610 --> 00:40:53.650
My client made the trip for nothing.

00:40:53.810 --> 00:40:56.650
Oh, come on. You didn't really come here...

00:40:56.720 --> 00:40:58.020
just to complain about that, did you?

00:40:58.150 --> 00:40:59.650
Yes. I mean, no.

00:40:59.820 --> 00:41:03.360
Otherwise, what reason would I have to come to a neighbourhood like this?

00:41:03.490 --> 00:41:05.730
You were curious, weren't you? "What's this about now?"

00:41:05.830 --> 00:41:08.160
"What kind of trick is he trying to pull?"

00:41:08.300 --> 00:41:11.170
You couldn't stand the suspense, so you came running.

00:41:11.330 --> 00:41:15.940
- No. - It is what it is.

00:41:17.270 --> 00:41:18.870
You know what my nickname is, don't you?

00:41:19.170 --> 00:41:20.170
Imoogi.

00:41:20.240 --> 00:41:24.280
There's only one thing in this world that the great Imoogi can't defeat.

00:41:25.380 --> 00:41:27.580
- And what's that? - A troublemaker.

00:41:27.720 --> 00:41:31.250
- Excuse me? - My client's simply a troublemaker.

00:41:31.320 --> 00:41:33.650
And I'm just as pissed off about it.

00:41:35.590 --> 00:41:39.630
I got backstabbed, just like you.

00:41:42.830 --> 00:41:45.000
A troublemaker is a troublemaker,

00:41:45.430 --> 00:41:47.800
and a betrayal is a betrayal.

00:41:53.140 --> 00:41:54.840
But where on earth could he have gone?

00:41:56.480 --> 00:41:58.080
Where could he have gone that made him skip...

00:41:58.150 --> 00:41:59.550
the Domestic Affairs Investigation?

00:41:59.550 --> 00:42:02.280
And just why would he go there?

00:42:02.580 --> 00:42:03.920
Why do I need to know any of that?

00:42:04.150 --> 00:42:05.420
And that's your problem.

00:42:06.950 --> 00:42:08.660
An Imoogi is an Imoogi,

00:42:08.720 --> 00:42:11.760
and Jeon Chi Hyun still has a long way to go.

00:42:16.760 --> 00:42:17.770
Mi Young.

00:42:18.070 --> 00:42:20.940
- Yes? - CEO Ji just came in.

00:42:21.240 --> 00:42:23.370
- What? - I think...

00:42:23.370 --> 00:42:25.510
he got back from that fishing spot.

00:42:25.970 --> 00:42:26.970
The fishing spot?

00:42:38.420 --> 00:42:39.920
You went to that fishing spot?

00:42:40.890 --> 00:42:41.890
Yes.

00:42:42.720 --> 00:42:43.720
Right.

00:42:44.330 --> 00:42:46.630
Whether you attend the Domestic Affairs Investigation...

00:42:46.630 --> 00:42:47.630
or not...

00:42:48.200 --> 00:42:49.600
is up to you.

00:42:58.670 --> 00:43:02.680
By the way, Calvin...

00:43:03.810 --> 00:43:06.010
offered me the CEO position for his new venture.

00:43:09.380 --> 00:43:11.290
Calvin's starting a wedding business,

00:43:12.520 --> 00:43:13.690
and he asked me to help him.

00:43:17.090 --> 00:43:18.490
Well, good for you.

00:43:19.690 --> 00:43:22.700
Then once the trial is over, everything will be settled.

00:43:26.930 --> 00:43:28.440
We're almost at the end,

00:43:28.570 --> 00:43:32.610
so let's not hurt each other anymore and just end this well.

00:43:33.210 --> 00:43:34.340
That's all I want...

00:43:35.810 --> 00:43:36.810
now.

00:43:44.890 --> 00:43:46.920
(Fishing Spot)

00:43:49.320 --> 00:43:51.230
Why do you think he went to that fishing spot?

00:43:51.930 --> 00:43:54.900
- Excuse me? - After skipping the investigation,

00:43:54.960 --> 00:43:57.700
why a fishing spot of all places?

00:44:00.970 --> 00:44:04.470
To give up on everything and clear his head?

00:44:07.840 --> 00:44:08.840
No...

00:44:10.740 --> 00:44:13.680
Imoogi wouldn't have said that for no reason.

00:44:16.120 --> 00:44:18.490
(Fishing Spot)

00:44:23.960 --> 00:44:24.960
Counsellor,

00:44:26.130 --> 00:44:28.930
today is the 22nd, right?

00:44:30.260 --> 00:44:31.270
Yes.

00:44:32.230 --> 00:44:33.230
Why do you ask?

00:44:40.980 --> 00:44:43.580
- Finalize the shoot schedule. - Okay.

00:44:43.640 --> 00:44:45.550
And Yeong Yu, please coordinate...

00:44:45.550 --> 00:44:47.920
with the studio on the concept and send it over.

00:45:07.500 --> 00:45:10.370
(Recent Destination)

00:45:12.810 --> 00:45:14.640
(Recent Destination: Fishing Spot)

00:46:01.660 --> 00:46:02.660
Here to do some fishing?

00:46:02.960 --> 00:46:05.930
No. I was just looking around.

00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:13.330
See that? Looks like just a bare branch, doesn't it?

00:46:13.670 --> 00:46:17.200
It's not. That's an azalea tree.

00:46:18.510 --> 00:46:19.610
An azalea?

00:46:19.810 --> 00:46:21.510
When spring comes, you wouldn't believe...

00:46:21.580 --> 00:46:24.310
how beautifully the azaleas bloom here.

00:46:24.980 --> 00:46:26.750
About three years ago, I think?

00:46:27.080 --> 00:46:30.280
A tall, handsome young man came and planted it.

00:46:30.650 --> 00:46:34.290
I believe his daughter's name was Dallae.

00:46:44.870 --> 00:46:47.300
From what I heard, he had a very sad story.

00:46:48.700 --> 00:46:52.240
I think the baby died before she was even born.

00:46:57.510 --> 00:47:00.150
He brought the baby's ashes, barely a handful,

00:47:00.710 --> 00:47:02.720
and asked if it would be okay to bury it over there.

00:47:03.180 --> 00:47:05.720
He begged and begged with a face that looked like death.

00:47:07.050 --> 00:47:10.590
And he buried it right there?

00:47:11.330 --> 00:47:14.700
The young man said if his child had been born,

00:47:15.100 --> 00:47:18.000
she would have been born around the time the azaleas bloom.

00:47:20.900 --> 00:47:23.670
By any chance, did that young man...

00:47:25.010 --> 00:47:26.270
visit today as well?

00:47:26.470 --> 00:47:28.140
Yes, he did.

00:47:29.140 --> 00:47:31.410
But isn't it strange?

00:47:31.550 --> 00:47:33.210
He never seems to visit...

00:47:33.210 --> 00:47:34.520
when the azaleas are actually blooming.

00:47:35.120 --> 00:47:37.990
And they're such beautiful flowers.

00:47:55.340 --> 00:47:58.140
I had no choice because of the seal.

00:47:58.270 --> 00:48:01.140
Does that give you the right to go through someone's things?

00:48:01.480 --> 00:48:03.840
I wasn't trying to go through your things.

00:48:03.840 --> 00:48:05.110
Apologise.

00:48:08.250 --> 00:48:10.720
He didn't mention the brooch,

00:48:11.220 --> 00:48:13.990
and he just kept getting angry.

00:48:16.590 --> 00:48:18.130
Did you ever find it?

00:48:18.890 --> 00:48:20.860
No, I never did.

00:48:21.600 --> 00:48:24.160
But why are you asking about the brooch all of a sudden?

00:48:24.400 --> 00:48:29.540
Mi Young still hasn't found the brooch.

00:48:30.100 --> 00:48:31.970
I'm going to prove...

00:48:32.270 --> 00:48:35.580
that you were the one who tried to push me off that cliff.

00:48:37.480 --> 00:48:38.480
Gosh.

00:48:39.380 --> 00:48:42.180
And what was that all about?

00:48:43.350 --> 00:48:46.390
Gosh, my head is about to explode.

00:49:14.720 --> 00:49:16.280
So that was today...

00:49:17.080 --> 00:49:18.190
Time flies.

00:49:19.150 --> 00:49:21.460
Please pray hard for me, Father.

00:49:22.190 --> 00:49:23.320
Don't you worry about that.

00:49:24.160 --> 00:49:25.690
Why do you look so worn out?

00:49:27.230 --> 00:49:28.230
Have you eaten?

00:49:30.500 --> 00:49:32.730
This won't do. Let's go get something to eat.

00:49:33.670 --> 00:49:34.670
Father...

00:49:35.900 --> 00:49:36.970
Rather than that,

00:49:37.900 --> 00:49:40.010
I'd like to talk with you, Father.

00:49:40.640 --> 00:49:42.280
Can I make a confession?

00:49:46.080 --> 00:49:47.380
For some reason today,

00:49:49.350 --> 00:49:52.420
I feel all choked up here, and I can't breathe.

00:49:53.390 --> 00:49:54.860
I thought if I confessed to you, Father,

00:49:55.160 --> 00:49:56.690
I might feel a little better.

00:49:57.220 --> 00:50:00.130
Then go on in. I'll get ready and join you.

00:50:00.790 --> 00:50:01.800
Yes, Father.

00:50:12.910 --> 00:50:14.470
(Confessional)

00:50:14.540 --> 00:50:17.010
(Penitent, Priest, Penitent)

00:50:23.350 --> 00:50:25.150
(Confessional)

00:50:30.190 --> 00:50:32.830
(Penitent, Priest, Penitent)

00:50:44.300 --> 00:50:45.570
I wish to confess...

00:50:47.610 --> 00:50:49.010
my sin.

00:50:50.710 --> 00:50:51.710
Lord,

00:50:53.150 --> 00:50:54.180
today, I...

00:50:55.620 --> 00:50:57.150
confess my weakness...

00:50:59.420 --> 00:51:00.990
and my selfishness.

00:51:03.720 --> 00:51:04.730
All this time,

00:51:06.290 --> 00:51:07.560
I've selfishly hurt...

00:51:08.930 --> 00:51:10.230
my husband...

00:51:11.400 --> 00:51:14.840
over and over again.

00:51:17.100 --> 00:51:20.710
I confess what I've done and deeply repent.

00:51:23.180 --> 00:51:24.180
I...

00:51:27.510 --> 00:51:29.380
thought I was the only one hurting,

00:51:32.850 --> 00:51:34.220
that I was the only one in agony,

00:51:35.590 --> 00:51:37.090
the only one to be pitied,

00:51:40.490 --> 00:51:42.530
and the only one in pain.

00:51:46.870 --> 00:51:47.870
But...

00:51:49.940 --> 00:51:51.370
that wasn't true.

00:51:53.570 --> 00:51:56.280
My husband was hurting just as much as me...

00:51:57.840 --> 00:51:58.850
No,

00:51:59.980 --> 00:52:03.850
even more than me.

00:52:06.820 --> 00:52:09.160
The reason I couldn't see his pain...

00:52:11.490 --> 00:52:13.590
was because he remained silent.

00:52:16.260 --> 00:52:17.930
To protect his weak wife,

00:52:19.830 --> 00:52:23.770
my husband couldn't even once cry out properly.

00:52:25.010 --> 00:52:26.010
Like that,

00:52:27.270 --> 00:52:30.110
he swallowed his pain.

00:52:30.610 --> 00:52:31.910
I said don't.

00:52:31.980 --> 00:52:34.210
I said don't.

00:52:34.280 --> 00:52:36.080
I want to die.

00:52:36.080 --> 00:52:37.280
Hey, Baek Mi Young!

00:52:49.430 --> 00:52:51.830
I want to die.

00:52:53.530 --> 00:52:55.670
Unlike me, who was busy screaming,

00:52:56.200 --> 00:52:58.340
(Cremation in progress)

00:52:58.410 --> 00:53:00.370
(Cremation Room)

00:53:00.510 --> 00:53:01.510
my husband...

00:53:03.340 --> 00:53:04.850
held in the pain...

00:53:07.080 --> 00:53:08.220
the more it hurt.

00:53:08.980 --> 00:53:11.990
The more it hurt, the more he turned inward,

00:53:12.950 --> 00:53:15.060
withdrawing deeper into himself.

00:53:17.520 --> 00:53:18.530
Even after...

00:53:20.560 --> 00:53:22.260
burying Dallae there,

00:53:25.370 --> 00:53:26.370
my husband...

00:53:28.470 --> 00:53:30.740
didn't go back...

00:53:32.710 --> 00:53:34.140
when the azaleas were in bloom.

00:53:35.510 --> 00:53:39.910
I know that my husband couldn't bear to face...

00:53:41.750 --> 00:53:43.250
those beautiful flowers...

00:53:45.920 --> 00:53:47.420
all too well.

00:53:50.620 --> 00:53:51.630
Because...

00:53:53.890 --> 00:53:54.900
we...

00:53:56.730 --> 00:53:58.370
are connected...

00:54:01.000 --> 00:54:03.270
by the single bond of Dallae.

00:54:05.370 --> 00:54:06.370
Because we...

00:54:09.380 --> 00:54:10.580
were husband and wife,

00:54:11.950 --> 00:54:13.410
and we were her parents.

00:54:20.350 --> 00:54:22.790
Lord, please...

00:54:25.190 --> 00:54:26.190
do not...

00:54:28.160 --> 00:54:29.600
forgive my sins.

00:54:39.010 --> 00:54:40.910
(Penitent, Priest, Penitent)

00:54:45.310 --> 00:54:48.680
(Penitent, Priest, Penitent)

00:57:02.020 --> 00:57:03.480
Calvin...

00:57:04.980 --> 00:57:07.420
offered me the CEO position for his new venture.

00:57:09.160 --> 00:57:11.120
Calvin's starting a wedding business,

00:57:12.330 --> 00:57:13.530
and he asked me for help.

00:58:00.010 --> 00:58:01.510
We're almost at the end,

00:58:01.610 --> 00:58:05.550
so let's not hurt each other anymore and just end this well.

00:58:06.250 --> 00:58:07.380
All I want...

00:58:09.120 --> 00:58:10.280
is just that.

00:58:51.560 --> 00:58:53.860
What are you doing here at this hour?

00:58:58.230 --> 00:58:59.230
Won Ho.

00:59:00.830 --> 00:59:02.470
Let's go together sometime.

00:59:05.040 --> 00:59:06.640
When the azaleas bloom,

00:59:08.910 --> 00:59:10.840
let's make sure we go see them together.

00:59:15.380 --> 00:59:16.680
That's what I came to say.

00:59:34.230 --> 00:59:35.300
Let's go.

00:59:39.370 --> 00:59:40.640
Yes, let's go.

00:59:44.940 --> 00:59:46.280
Let's go together...

00:59:49.280 --> 00:59:51.950
and be sure to visit Dallae.

01:01:34.350 --> 01:01:37.260
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

01:01:38.760 --> 01:01:39.860
Do you think he actually wants...

01:01:40.390 --> 01:01:42.530
to get back together with me?

01:01:42.600 --> 01:01:44.730
- What do you mean, risky? - Do you think her feelings...

01:01:45.100 --> 01:01:46.800
will change that easily, all of a sudden?

01:01:46.900 --> 01:01:49.440
You know how much my Won Ho loves children, don't you?

01:01:49.500 --> 01:01:52.840
Mi Young, I want to spend the rest of my life with you.

01:01:54.140 --> 01:01:55.140
You know what?

01:01:55.210 --> 01:01:56.880
I can tear CEO Ji and CEO Baek apart...

01:01:57.140 --> 01:01:58.910
at any time.

01:01:59.310 --> 01:02:00.750
Then I have no choice but to see this through.

01:02:01.050 --> 01:02:02.220
It's not too late.

01:02:02.820 --> 01:02:05.180
And you still have a chance.